.TH LARZ 1 "LarzOS" "LarzOS" "LarzOS Manual"
.SH NAME
larz \- the LarzOS command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B larz
.I verb
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B larz
is the single entry point for running a LarzOS machine: installing software,
previewing and applying the system spec
.RI ( /etc/larzos/system.lz ),
talking to the AI model router, and checking the system over. It is a thin,
LarzOS\-styled front end to
.BR apt\-get (8),
.BR larz-system (8)
and
.BR larz-aid (8),
which all remain usable directly.
.SH VERBS
.TP
.B install " \fIpkg\fR..."
Install packages.
.TP
.B remove " \fIpkg\fR..."
Remove packages.
.TP
.B search " \fItext\fR"
Search available packages.
.TP
.B update
Refresh the package lists.
.TP
.B upgrade
Update every installed package.
.TP
.B list
List installed packages.
.TP
.B plan " [\fIsystem.lz\fR]"
Show what applying the spec would change. Touches nothing.
.TP
.B apply " [\fIsystem.lz\fR]"
Converge the machine onto the spec.
.TP
.B rollback
Re\-apply the previous spec.
.TP
.B status
Drift and a one\-line summary.
.TP
.B ai " \fItext\fR"
Ask the model router. \fBlarz ai route \fItask\fR reports which backend serves a task.
.TP
.B doctor
Check identity, engine, AI router, package sources, disk and services.
.TP
.B rebrand " [status|apply|restore]"
Re\-assert (or remove) the LarzOS identity.
.TP
.B version
Show component versions.
.TP
.B apt " \fIargs\fR"
Pass \fIargs\fR straight to \fBapt\-get\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/larzos/system.lz
The machine, described in Larzscript.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR larz-system (8),
.BR larz-aid (8),
.BR larz-rebrand (8)
